# clang-format configuration for the C sources.
#
# This captures the prevailing house style: 4-space indentation, no tabs,
# functions with the opening brace on its own line and control statements with
# the brace on the same line (the Linux brace convention), and a 100-column
# soft limit.
#
# Apply it to a file with:
#   clang-format -i src/foo.c include/foo.h
#
# The tree predates this file, so not every existing file is clean yet; the
# config is the reference for new and edited code.
---
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
IndentWidth: 4
TabWidth: 4
UseTab: Never
ColumnLimit: 100
BreakBeforeBraces: Linux
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: All
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: Never
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: false
PointerAlignment: Right
DerivePointerAlignment: false
SortIncludes: Never
SpaceBeforeParens: ControlStatements
AlignAfterOpenBracket: Align
